=== Prompt ===
Who is Pikachu?

=== Response ===
Pikachu is a fictional character and the official mascot of Pokémon, a media franchise managed by The Pokémon Company. Pikachu is a small, yellow, electric mouse-like Pokémon that is one of the most recognizable and popular characters in the franchise. It was created by Game Freak's Satoshi Tajiri and Ken Sugimori for the game Pokémon Red and Green (later released as Pokémon Red and Blue in North America).

Pikachu is a quadruped rodent-like Pokémon with a yellow body, two round, red ears on its head, two round, black eyes, and a long, pointed tail. Its body is covered in short, yellow fur, and it has two round, pinkish-red cheeks on either side of its face. Pikachu's most distinctive feature is the electric sacs on the back of its body, which it can use to store and discharge electric energy.

Pikachu is a popular character in the Pokémon franchise due to its cute appearance and its electric-type abilities. It is often depicted as the companion of the main character in the Pokémon games and the Pokémon animated series, and it is also featured in a variety of merchandise, including toys, clothing, and other items. Pikachu has become a cultural icon and is recognized by people around the world.

